== The Warden's Checklist

A living endgame checklist. Work top to bottom; loop the bottom rows whenever a session needs direction.

=== Short-Term (per session)

- [ ] Eat dango for the fight ahead.
- [ ] Restock + loadout check (mega potions, whetstone, matchup items).
- [ ] Confirm the investigation list has a level you can climb.
- [ ] Check Meowcenaries / Argosy routes are still useful.
- [ ] One new monster read: which attack did you misjudge last time?

=== Medium-Term (per rank tier)

- [ ] Armor upgraded to tier cap (spheres spent, not hoarded).
- [ ] Main weapon augmented with the next affordable tier.
- [ ] Comfort core still adequate for the current monster tier.
- [ ] Talisman melding running — materials spent, not banked.
- [ ] At least one elemental set drafted for the current big weakness.

=== Long-Term (the quarry's final lessons)

- [ ] All risen elders defeated at least once.
- [ ] One weapon fully augmented to your satisfaction.
- [ ] Layered armor + weapon set that looks like *you*.
- [ ] A support set built and actually played in multiplayer.
- [ ] Special/hazard quests: the quarry's hardest tiers, beaten for the story of it.

=== When in Doubt

- Hitting a wall? It is *armor upgrades, element matching, or a tell you are not reading* — never "keep grinding the same thing."
- Bored? Switch weapons for a session. The quarry does not care how you hunt it, only that you do.
- Burnt out? Stop. The quarry will still be here tomorrow; the resentment won't survive the break.

#note[
  The endgame is a marathon by design. The warden who finishes is not the one who played the most — it is the one who played *varied*, *deliberately*, and *without grinding the joy out of it*.
]
